 - 2026-06-15: PHASE A2 (HEADLINE BUILD, gated_on A1 arc_pool_grown) -- TRAIN the FULL permutation-invariant SET-ENCODER cross-candidate aggregator on the grown pool. .392's aggregator (exp4231) was an AUGMENTED-LOGISTIC form (explicit set-summary features bolted onto per-candidate logistic regression); the .392 SOTA-ingestion (exp4238) flagged that 'explicit summary features were not enough' and named the next lever: a TRUE permutation-invariant candidate-SET encoder with inter-candidate attention over all grids and vote basins (Set-Encoder 2404.06912; MSV 2603.03417 cross-sequence). Train a DeepSets/attention set-encoder that scores each candidate CONDITIONED on the full per-task candidate set, with the calibrated imbalance-aware loss (2509.19681: class-weighted/focal + stratified-balanced minibatches + temperature/isotonic calibration), OUT-OF-FOLD (held-out-task split), verifier_is_oracle=false. ABLATE against the .392 augmented-logistic aggregator on the SAME split. Report off-fold AUROC (set-encoder vs augmented-logistic) + aggregator_trained + learned_verifier_path. Honest no-gain-over-logistic is COMPLETE and still feeds A3. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete_arc_set_encoder_no_gain_over_logistic_auroc0.9633; results/experiment_4244_arc_set_encoder_aggregator_build.json
 - 2026-06-15: PHASE A3 (THE HEADLINE GATE, gated_on A2 aggregator_trained) -- does the FULL SET-ENCODER aggregator BEAT majority vote OFF-ORACLE on ARC at power? On a HELD-OUT ARC split (disjoint from A2 folds, target N>=40), rerank with the A2 Set-Encoder (verifier_is_oracle=false; does NOT execute demos) vs majority-vote vs a MATCHED no-verifier control (same candidates/budget) vs oracle@K (the positive-control ceiling) vs a MARGIN-TRIGGERED override (2606.04323: override vote ONLY when the set-encoder margin clears a pre-registered threshold tuned on the A2 fold). The LOAD-BEARING gate: set_encoder@1 - vote@1, bootstrap CI95 EXCLUDES 0 AND headroom exists. YES -> the FIRST ARC oracle-distinct win (closes GAP-3-ties-vote on the north-star domain; justifies activating the gated DiffusionGemma bet). TIES-at-power-on-the-grown-pool -> a much STRONGER null than .392 (now the data-sparsity confound is removed -> a real selection bound). No-headroom -> uninformative (FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK). (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: arc_oracle_distinct_set_encoder_beats_vote; results/experiment_4245_arc_set_encoder_beats_vote.json
 - 2026-06-15: PHASE A4 (HEADLINE CONFIRMATION; independent) -- CONFIRM the .392 code oracle-distinct win generalizes on a SECOND balanced code corpus. .392 (exp4233) showed a LEARNED no-execution code pass-predictor beats vote (+3.1pp, CI95 [0.006,0.0625], n=160) on ONE candidate pool (the verifier_reward_3arm corpora). A single-corpus +3.1pp is a real but THIN win. Replicate the SAME oracle-distinct gate (learned pass-predictor over candidate code text + cross-candidate agreement, NO test execution at inference, verifier_is_oracle=false) on a DIFFERENT cached code candidate pool (MBPP / EvalPlus / a second HumanEval ensemble eval). predictor@1 vs vote@1 vs matched control vs oracle@K, task-level bootstrap CI95-excl-0, N as large as the cached pool allows. Replicates -> the code oracle-distinct win is robust (strengthens the headline; corroborates ARC if A3 wins, isolates ARC-specificity if A3 ties). Honest no-replication is COMPLETE (the .392 win was corpus-specific). STOP re-running CIRCULAR code-execution selection. (⚠️ Blocked) — honest_verdict=blocked_code_second_corpus_missing; results/experiment_4246_code_oracle_distinct_replication.json
+- 2026-06-15: PHASE B1 (OWED pivot; RETIRE live-LoRA + OFFLINE harness smoke) -- the live-LoRA verifier-as-reward path has now failed 6x on INFRA (exp4198 bg-death, exp4199 gate-block, exp4211 PEFT attach, exp4222/exp4223 DURATION short-circuits, exp4234 blocked_lora_training_cannot_run_in_window) and NEVER reached science; the operator's accumulate-floor (3 consecutive no-usable windows) is long since met. RETIRE the live-LoRA path (live_lora_retired BARE bool=true) and PIVOT to an OFFLINE reward-weighted form that FITS THE WINDOW: precompute per-example reward weights from the intact A/B/C corpora, then run a BOUNDED offline reward-weighted LoRA-SFT (RAFT/reward-weighted-regression/filtered-BC -- a finite, deterministic-step training, NOT open-ended live RL). SMOKE it as a POSITIVE CONTROL that PROVES real training: LoRA attaches with >0 trainable params on a small NON-Qwen base via AutoModelForCausalLM, >=20 REAL optimizer steps on a fixture, loss MOVES (final<initial), wall-clock exceeds a plausibility floor. harness_smoke_passed BARE bool. NO full A/B/C here (that is B2). NO TRM. (⚠️ Blocked) — honest_verdict=blocked_offline_reward_weighted_training_cannot_run_in_window; results/experiment_4247_verifier_reward_offline_harness_retire_livelora.json
